+# Agent Note: Per-teammate model selection in Agent Teams spawn
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-02-agent-teams-spawn-model.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Every Agent Teams teammate inherited the Team Lead's model. `spawn_teammate` had no `model` parameter, so a reviewer and a producer could not run on different models. Heterogeneous-reviewer grill acceptance — where the reviewer reviews a producer's work on a distinct model so it does not self-approve — therefore could not be expressed per role. The request type carried only the continuable-child `provider` (the `spawn`/`fork` mechanism name), never the LLM model.
+
+## Decision
+
+`spawn_teammate` now accepts two optional route fields: `model` (a model id string) and `reasoning_effort` (a `ReasoningEffortId`). Both are optional and both default to inheriting the Team Lead's route. `SpawnTeammateRequest` gained `model?` and `reasoningEffort?`; `TeamRoster.spawnAdmitted` forwards them through the existing `SubagentStartRequest.agentOptions` slot, so the per-child override path in `resolveChildAgentOptions` (subagent child-agent) merges them over the parent's route, exactly as it already did for any explicit `agentOptions`.
+
+The tool schema exposes `model` and `reasoning_effort` to the model; an omitted `model` produces an empty `agentOptions`, which keeps `resolveChildAgentOptions` inheriting the Lead's route unchanged. The runtime member view already reads the live child's `options.model`, so a spawned teammate running on its own model reports it through `list_agents` with no extra plumbing.
+
+Backward compatibility is exact: a call without `model`/`reasoning_effort` behaves identically to before the change, because `agentOptions` stays empty (or contains only what the caller named).
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Add a free-standing `model` argument that flows to the continuable descriptor request directly.** Rejected because the subagent request already owns `agentOptions` as the single per-child route override channel; adding a parallel argument would duplicate the merge and the route-changed reasoning-effort clearing logic.
+
+**Let the caller pass a provider in the same tool.** Rejected as out of scope: the teammate's LLM provider continues to be inherited, and changing provider is a different concern from giving a reviewer a distinct model.
+
+**Treat an omitted `reasoning_effort` with a named `model` as "inherit the parent's effort".** Rejected because `resolveChildAgentOptions` already clears route-owned effort when the route changes without naming one, letting the selected model resolve its own default; preserving that behavior keeps model selection consistent with the subagent route machinery.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A teammate can now run on a distinct model from the Lead, which is what lets heterogeneous grill acceptance assign a reviewer and a producer to different models.
+- The model route remains subject to the delegation executor's authorization policy: an explicit `model`/`reasoning_effort` is still rejected when its effective route falls outside the Session allowlist. This change surfaces a route choice, it does not bypass authorization.
+- `followup_task` and `send_message` carry no model; a teammate's route is fixed at spawn time, so a follow-up turn reuses the model the teammate was created with. The fork provider still exposes no route selection, as documented in the model-route notes.
+- No new peer dependency was added: `AgentOptions` is already a peer of `tool-agent-team`, and the reasoning-effort boundary cast reuses the established `ReasoningEffortId` convention.
+
+## Related
+
+- [agent-teams](2026-08-05-agent-teams.md) — the umbrella Agent Teams decision this extends.
+- [model-selected subagent routes](2026-08-18-model-selected-subagent-routes.md) — the subagent route selection machinery that `agentOptions` targets.
+- [user-authorized subagent model routes](2026-08-24-user-authorized-subagent-model-routes.md) — the executor authorization policy that still governs an explicit model route.
